      "body": "## Summary\n\n- keep the raw text for string-typed GLM4 tool arguments emitted as bare scalars (123, true, null): the JSON-coerced int/bool/None hit the caller's `str()` fallback and came out as Python spellings (\"True\", \"None\") instead of the model's exact text\n- the glm47 twin needs no change; its caller already falls back to the raw arg_value when the parsed value is not a string\n\nFixes #42133.\n\n## To verify\n\n- `python -m pytest test/registered/unit/function_call/test_function_call_parser.py -k glm` passes except `TestGlm47MoeDetector::test_get_model_structural_tag`, which fails on upstream/main as well\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:hourglass_flowing_sand: [Run #37001385537](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37001385537)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:hourglass_flowing_sand: [Run #37001384854](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37001384854)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:hourglass_flowing_sand: [Run #37001385518](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37001385518)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->\n",
      "changedFiles": 2,
      "comments": {
        "nodes": [
          {
            "author": {
              "__typename": "Bot",
              "login": "gemini-code-assist"
            },
            "body": "> [!WARNING]\n> You have reached your daily quota limit. Please wait up to 24 hours and I will start processing your requests again!",
            "createdAt": "2026-06-13T01:39:55Z",
            "databaseId": 4697005118,
            "updatedAt": "2026-06-13T01:39:55Z",
            "url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/28114#issuecomment-4697005118"
          },
          {
            "author": {
              "__typename": "User",
              "login": "he-yufeng"
            },
            "body": "Friendly ping — this preserves GLM string request IDs that contain underscores (they were getting mangled). Small and self-contained. Would appreciate a review when someone has a moment.",
            "createdAt": "2026-07-13T05:12:33Z",
            "databaseId": 4954645458,
            "updatedAt": "2026-07-13T05:12:33Z",
            "url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/28114#issuecomment-4954645458"
          },
          {
            "author": {
              "__typename": "User",
              "login": "he-yufeng"
            },
            "body": "Reworked onto current main. The June version guarded the ast.literal_eval fallback; main has since grown strategy 2.5 (raw text for string-typed non-JSON) via #30644, which covers the underscore-grouped case, but strategies 1 and 2 still coerce an unquoted scalar for a string-typed param: json.loads(\"123\") returns int 123 straight into a string argument. The guard now sits at both JSON-success exits: string-typed and not a string means keep the raw text. Verified locally with the extracted parser (upstream returns int 123 / bool True on the witnesses, this branch returns the raw text); the registered parser suite covers the new cases in CI since it needs the full env.",
            "createdAt": "2026-08-19T00:22:07Z",
            "databaseId": 5335928576,
            "updatedAt": "2026-08-19T00:22:07Z",
            "url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/28114#issuecomment-5335928576"
          },
          {
            "author": {
              "__typename": "User",
              "login": "he-yufeng"
            },
            "body": "Re-checked against current main today: the coercion still mangles id-shaped strings. For a string-typed parameter, a JSON value that parses as a number gets `str(parsed_value)`, so `1e3` comes out as `1000.0` and `1.50` as `1.5`; the model's literal text is lost even though the schema asked for a string. The diff keeps the raw text whenever the schema type is string and the parsed value is not a string, in both GLM-4 MoE detectors, with regression tests. Still applies cleanly. Any objection to landing it?\n",
            "createdAt": "2026-09-11T13:57:20Z",
            "databaseId": 5635497976,
            "updatedAt": "2026-09-11T13:57:20Z",
            "url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/28114#issuecomment-5635497976"
          },
          {
            "author": {
              "__typename": "User",
              "login": "he-yufeng"
            },
            "body": "Re-verified on current main (93809202a3): `parse_arguments` in `glm4_moe_detector.py` still returns the JSON-coerced value for a string-typed parameter whose model output is a bare scalar (123, true, null), so the caller's `str()` fallback still emits Python spellings instead of the model's raw text. The newer Strategy 2.5 covers non-JSON strings but not this case. Four months in the queue; could a maintainer add the run-ci label?\n",
            "createdAt": "2026-10-12T22:22:04Z",
            "databaseId": 6133704997,
            "updatedAt": "2026-10-12T22:22:04Z",
            "url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/28114#issuecomment-6133704997"
          }
